   "reference": {
    "title": "WHO CNS5 meningioma integrated grading & molecular overrule",
    "intro": "WHO CNS5 treats meningioma as a single tumour type with 15 subtypes and assigns CNS WHO grade 1, 2, or 3 using combined histologic and molecular criteria. TERT promoter mutation or CDKN2A/B homozygous deletion automatically assigns CNS WHO grade 3 regardless of histology.",
    "note": "Photomicrographs are from Wikimedia Commons under open Creative Commons licences. ExpertPath pages open with your own ExpertPath login; the app holds none of their images.",
    "groups": [
     {
      "heading": "WHO CNS5 grading rules & key IHC/molecular associations",
      "points": [
       "CNS WHO grade 2: 4–19 mitoses/10 HPF (1.6 mm2), OR brain invasion (irregular tongues into GFAP+ brain parenchyma), OR >= 3 of 5 atypical features (sheeting, hypercellularity, small cells with high N:C, prominent nucleoli, spontaneous necrosis), OR chordoid / clear cell subtype.",
       "CNS WHO grade 3: >= 20 mitoses/10 HPF, OR frank anaplasia (carcinoma/melanoma/sarcoma-like), OR TERT promoter mutation, OR CDKN2A/B homozygous deletion. (Papillary and rhabdoid are no longer grade 3 on morphology alone.)",
       "IHC/molecular: SSTR2A (most sensitive) and EMA positive; STAT6 negative (excludes solitary fibrous tumour); SMARCE1 loss in clear cell; BAP1 loss in aggressive rhabdoid/papillary; KLF4/TRAF7 in secretory."
      ],
      "links": [
       {
        "label": "ExpertPath: Meningioma",
        "url": "https://app.expertpath.com/"
       }
      ],
      "images": [
       {
        "src": "assets/reference/meningioma/mng_psammomatous.jpg",
        "caption": "Psammomatous meningioma: numerous concentrically laminated calcified psammoma bodies within meningothelial whorls (H&E).",
        "credit": "Jensflorian",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File%3ANP_psammomatous_meningioma_0002.jpg"
       },
